# Linting & formatting

- ESLint (flat config, `eslint.config.js`) is the source of truth for code-quality rules; Prettier only handles formatting. Never let ESLint rules and Prettier fight over formatting — `eslint-config-prettier` disables all stylistic ESLint rules that would conflict.
- Run `eslint --fix` and `prettier --write` before considering any task done. Do not leave lint errors or warnings unresolved — fix them, don't disable the rule, unless there's a documented reason (inline `// eslint-disable-next-line <rule> -- reason`).
- Tailwind classes must stay sorted by `prettier-plugin-tailwindcss` — never manually reorder classes to "look right"; trust the plugin's canonical order.

## Required dependencies

```
eslint
typescript-eslint
eslint-plugin-react
eslint-plugin-react-hooks
eslint-plugin-jsx-a11y
eslint-config-prettier
prettier
prettier-plugin-tailwindcss
```

## `eslint.config.js` (flat config, ESLint 9+)

```js
import js from '@eslint/js';
import tseslint from 'typescript-eslint';
import react from 'eslint-plugin-react';
import reactHooks from 'eslint-plugin-react-hooks';
import jsxA11y from 'eslint-plugin-jsx-a11y';
import prettierConfig from 'eslint-config-prettier';

export default tseslint.config(
  { ignores: ['dist', 'build', 'node_modules'] },
  js.configs.recommended,
  ...tseslint.configs.recommended,
  {
    files: ['**/*.{ts,tsx}'],
    plugins: {
      react,
      'react-hooks': reactHooks,
      'jsx-a11y': jsxA11y,
    },
    languageOptions: {
      parserOptions: {
        ecmaFeatures: { jsx: true },
      },
    },
    settings: {
      react: { version: 'detect' },
    },
    rules: {
      ...react.configs.recommended.rules,
      ...reactHooks.configs.recommended.rules,
      ...jsxA11y.configs.recommended.rules,

      'react/react-in-jsx-scope': 'off', // not needed with the new JSX transform
      'react/prop-types': 'off', // TypeScript handles this

      '@typescript-eslint/no-unused-vars': [
        'warn',
        { argsIgnorePattern: '^_', varsIgnorePattern: '^_' },
      ],
      '@typescript-eslint/no-explicit-any': 'error',
      '@typescript-eslint/consistent-type-imports': 'warn',

      'react-hooks/rules-of-hooks': 'error',
      'react-hooks/exhaustive-deps': 'warn',
    },
  },
  prettierConfig,
);
```

## `.prettierrc`

```json
{
  "semi": true,
  "singleQuote": true,
  "trailingComma": "all",
  "printWidth": 100,
  "tabWidth": 2,
  "plugins": ["prettier-plugin-tailwindcss"]
}
```

## `.prettierignore`

```
dist
build
node_modules
pnpm-lock.yaml
```

## Notes for Cursor

- When generating or editing code, always follow the rules above rather than default formatting — e.g. single quotes, trailing commas, no semicolon omission.
- Do not introduce unused variables/imports; if a variable is intentionally unused, prefix it with `_`.
- Prefer `import type { X } from '...'` for type-only imports (enforced by `consistent-type-imports`).
